"Go straight, turn left," I remember.
That is what the policeman said.
First, I walk straight.
Then I turn left early.
That is the wrong way.
This is a small street.
This is a big market.
There are many vegetable stalls here.
The street is very crowded.
I look around.
I am lost.
I do not see Marine Drive.
I see a woman there.
She has a cloth bag in her hand.
I go near her.
"Excuse me, I am lost," I say.
"Which is the way to Marine Drive?"
"Should I turn right?"
The woman looks at me.
She smiles kindly.
